{"study_accession":"PRJNA724934","secondary_study_accession":"SRP316225","title":"Distinct transcriptomic profiles of naive CD4+ T cells distinguish HIV-1 infected patients initiating antiretroviral treatment at acute or chronic phase of infection","description":"We analyzed the whole transcriptome characteristics of naive CD4+ T cells isolated from the blood of HIV-1 infected patients starting ART at acute or chronic phase of infection with the purpose of characterizing the impact of early ART initiation on naive T cell transcriptome integrity compared to non-infected individuals. In addition to quantifying the number of differentially expressed genes (DEGs) between the two groups of HIV-1 infected patients in relation to one another and to non-infected controls and their participation in biological processes we also characterize in detail DEGs involved in the process of apoptosis, inflammation and immune responses which play a pivotal role in dysfunctions identified during HIV-1 infection","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":39,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN18865353","study_accession":"PRJNA724934","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"EA","description":"EA","sex":"male","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-09-02","attributes":[["isolate","EA19"],["age","64"],["biomaterial_provider","Francesca Chiodi"],["sex","male"],["tissue","Blood"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR14320429","experiment_accession":"SRX10675578","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":38120036,"base_count":8672316459,"first_public":"2021-09-02","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: RNA-seq of homo sapiens: peripheral CD4+ naive T cells (early treated HIV-1)"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN18865354","study_accession":"PRJNA724934","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"EA","description":"EA","sex":"male","geo_sample":""